/T (In December 2022, the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework \(GBF\) was agreed by the parties to the United Nations Convention on Biological Diversity towards the goal of halting and reversing nature loss by 2030 w.r.t. the 2020 baseline and achieving full recovery by 2050 \(Fig.2\). The goal represents a fundamental shift in how societies and businesses should interact with the natural world, moving from minimizing harm to actively contributing to nature's recovery [3]. The Global Goal for Nature outlines three aims, set against a baseline of 2020, to:)
/E (In December 2022, the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework \(GBF\) was agreed by the parties to the United Nations Convention on Biological Diversity towards the goal of halting and reversing nature loss by 2030 w.r.t. the 2020 baseline and achieving full recovery by 2050 \(Fig.2\). The goal represents a fundamental shift in how societies and businesses should interact with the natural world, moving from minimizing harm to actively contributing to nature's recovery [3]. The Global Goal for Nature outlines three aims, set against a baseline of 2020, to:)
