/T (For high-impact and high-dependency industries i.e. mining, oil and gas, infrastructure, intensive agriculture \(right top and bottom quadrants in Fig. 4\), depend on resource extraction and land-use conversion at a large scale, thus, their full nature-positivity in the near term is operationally infeasible. The situation may not be so grim for the low dependency industries \(e.g. IT & Services\)  but feasibility in light of low to no accountancy, remains questionable. Unfortunately, low or not, feasibility can no longer afford to be inactive w.r.t. natural resources. )
/E (For high-impact and high-dependency industries i.e. mining, oil and gas, infrastructure, intensive agriculture \(right top and bottom quadrants in Fig. 4\), depend on resource extraction and land-use conversion at a large scale, thus, their full nature-positivity in the near term is operationally infeasible. The situation may not be so grim for the low dependency industries \(e.g. IT & Services\)  but feasibility in light of low to no accountancy, remains questionable. Unfortunately, low or not, feasibility can no longer afford to be inactive w.r.t. natural resources. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [29]
>>
