/T (India's policy landscape for nature-positive business is maturing considerably. The Securities and Exchange Board of India \(SEBI\) introduced Business Responsibility and Sustainability Reporting \(BRSR\) in 2021, requiring the top 1,000 listed companies to disclose environmental performance using standardized metrics [28]. BRSR Core, requiring third-party assurance, is being phased in: top 150 companies in FY 2023-24, expanding to all top 1,000 by FY 2026-27 \(Fig. 7 \) [29].)
/E (India's policy landscape for nature-positive business is maturing considerably. The Securities and Exchange Board of India \(SEBI\) introduced Business Responsibility and Sustainability Reporting \(BRSR\) in 2021, requiring the top 1,000 listed companies to disclose environmental performance using standardized metrics [28]. BRSR Core, requiring third-party assurance, is being phased in: top 150 companies in FY 2023-24, expanding to all top 1,000 by FY 2026-27 \(Fig. 7 \) [29].)
