/T (The World Bank estimates that while produced capital per person increased by more than 47% between 1995 and 2020, reflecting growth in infrastructure, manufactured assets and financial wealth whereas renewable natural capital per person declined by around 20%, driven by losses in biodiversity and ecosystem services [36]. This divergence suggests that economic expansion has been achieved alongside the erosion of the natural systems.)
/E (The World Bank estimates that while produced capital per person increased by more than 47% between 1995 and 2020, reflecting growth in infrastructure, manufactured assets and financial wealth whereas renewable natural capital per person declined by around 20%, driven by losses in biodiversity and ecosystem services [36]. This divergence suggests that economic expansion has been achieved alongside the erosion of the natural systems.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
