/S /H4
/P 220 0 R
/T (United Nations Environment Programme analyses indicate that this imbalance reflects a structural bias in conventional measures of economic progress, where gains in produced and financial capital mask the depletion of natural capital, leading to development pathways that underestimate long-term environmental and economic risks [37].)
