/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 222 0 R
/T (Recent years have seen growing recognition of nature as a form of critical infrastructure underpinning the global economy, prompting increased efforts to measure and value its role in order to safeguard long-term economic stability. A global survey of investors conducted by Pollination indicates that investors across regions, asset classes and sizes are increasingly focused on nature-related issues, both in terms of reducing portfolio risk and harm and in identifying emerging, bankable nature-positive investment opportunities [43]. There is a clear economic and financial opportunity. Research shows the nature-positive economy could be worth an additional $10.1 trillion in annual business value in 2030  [44].)
/E (Recent years have seen growing recognition of nature as a form of critical infrastructure underpinning the global economy, prompting increased efforts to measure and value its role in order to safeguard long-term economic stability. A global survey of investors conducted by Pollination indicates that investors across regions, asset classes and sizes are increasingly focused on nature-related issues, both in terms of reducing portfolio risk and harm and in identifying emerging, bankable nature-positive investment opportunities [43]. There is a clear economic and financial opportunity. Research shows the nature-positive economy could be worth an additional $10.1 trillion in annual business value in 2030  [44].)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
