496 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 224 0 R
/T (Case Study 1: Aditya Birla Group )
/E (Case Study 1: Aditya Birla Group )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
497 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 224 0 R
/E (Aditya Birla Group is a global conglomerate active in 22 industry sectors, including fashion, finance, and mining [45]. In 2021, the group added "waste to wealth for circularity" to its ESG priorities, noting that global raw-material extraction has more than doubled since 1990 [46]. The United Nations' International Resource Panel indicates that extraction and processing of materials cause 55% of global GHG emissions and more than 90% of land-use related biodiversity loss [47].)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
498 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 224 0 R
/E (Zero Waste to Landfill by 2030)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
499 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 224 0 R
/E (The group has set a company-wide goal of zero waste to landfill by 2030. To coordinate efforts, it formed a "Waste2Wealth for Circularity" working group with representatives from across its companies [48]. Three practical examples demonstrate progress:)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
500 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 224 0 R
/E (1. Industrial Symbiosis: Hindalco and UltraTech)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
501 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 224 0 R
/E (Hindalco converts bauxite residue \(red mud\) from aluminum production into a substitute for limestone used in cement. Over one million tonnes of processed red mud are supplied annually to UltraTech Cement, cutting the need for newly mined raw materials [49]. By 2020, Hindalco was supplying red mud to more than 40 cement plants. UltraTech reports that 20.6% of its total raw material use now comes from alternative materials, including red mud [50].)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
502 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 224 0 R
/E (2. Recycling at Scale: Novelis)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
503 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 224 0 R
/E (Novelis, part of the group, focuses on recycled aluminum for automotive and beverage packaging sectors. It runs closed-loop recycling systems and, as of FY24, 63% of Novelis's product inputs came from recycled material [51].)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
504 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 224 0 R
/E (3. Circular Products with Traceability: Liva Reviva)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
