/P 225 0 R
/T (Case Study 2: Holcim)
/E (Case Study 2: Holcim)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
512 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 225 0 R
/E (Holcim Group is a Swiss-based global building materials company with net sales of CHF 16.2 billion in 2024 and more than 45,000 employees in 44 markets [54]. Operating in a sector that depends heavily on limestone quarries, land and freshwater, Holcim formalized its nature-positive strategy in 2021, committing to restore and preserve biodiversity and freshwater ecosystems while measuring outcomes through a methodology developed with the International Union for Conservation of Nature \(IUCN\) [55].)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
513 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 225 0 R
/T (Governance and Strategy Integration)
/E (Governance and Strategy Integration)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
514 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 225 0 R
/E (In June 2022, Holcim issued a Group-wide Nature Policy setting binding expectations for employees, suppliers and business partners on efficient use of natural resources, quarry planning, rehabilitation and engagement with local communities [56]. The company was the first global building materials company to have both its 2030 and 2050 net-zero targets validated by the Science Based Targets initiative across Scope 1, 2 and 3 [57]. Its long-term incentive plans include sustainability performance metrics explicitly tied to climate, nature and circularity, linking executive pay to environmental progress [58].)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
515 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 225 0 R
/T (Progressive Quarry Rehabilitation)
/E (Progressive Quarry Rehabilitation)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
516 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 225 0 R
/E (Holcim has moved beyond compliance-based rehabilitation toward transformative restoration guided by science-based indicators such as its Biodiversity Indicator and Reporting System \(BIRS\). At the Yepes quarry in Spain, over 500 hectares of semi-arid land have been restored into a natural reserve hosting more than 360 plant species. A United Nations-backed study described Holcim as "one of the frontrunners in the business community when it comes to measuring biodiversity" [59].)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
517 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 225 0 R
/E (Holcim's Spanish operations have been used as a pilot in the UN NCAVES project to test natural capital accounting approaches for quarry restoration, demonstrating that the company is experimenting with integrating biodiversity values into decision-making rather than treating rehabilitation as a compliance add-on [60]. By 2022, all active quarries had rehabilitation plans in place and those in priority areas had biodiversity management plans [61].)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
