/T (India's business landscape is experiencing a shift in how environmental dependencies are understood and managed. The select case studies in this white paper Aditya Birla Group and Holcim demonstrate that nature-positive approaches are being implemented through industrial symbiosis in manufacturing and science-based biodiversity measurement in extractive industries.)
/E (India's business landscape is experiencing a shift in how environmental dependencies are understood and managed. The select case studies in this white paper Aditya Birla Group and Holcim demonstrate that nature-positive approaches are being implemented through industrial symbiosis in manufacturing and science-based biodiversity measurement in extractive industries.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
539 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 227 0 R
/T (The Aditya Birla Group's conversion of bauxite residue into cement inputs shows that waste can become a resource when coordination mechanisms exist between business units. Holcim's integration of biodiversity indicators into quarry rehabilitation demonstrates that restoration outcomes can be measured and reported using established scientific frameworks.)
/E (The Aditya Birla Group's conversion of bauxite residue into cement inputs shows that waste can become a resource when coordination mechanisms exist between business units. Holcim's integration of biodiversity indicators into quarry rehabilitation demonstrates that restoration outcomes can be measured and reported using established scientific frameworks.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
540 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 227 0 R
/T (However, implementation faces persistent challenges. Data gaps remain significant - companies often lack baseline information on species and habitats within their operational areas. Financial constraints limit access to nature-positive projects, particularly for MSMEs. Regulatory fragmentation across State Biodiversity Boards creates compliance uncertainty . The recognition of forest rights under the 2006 Act remains incomplete, leading to project delays.)
/E (However, implementation faces persistent challenges. Data gaps remain significant - companies often lack baseline information on species and habitats within their operational areas. Financial constraints limit access to nature-positive projects, particularly for MSMEs. Regulatory fragmentation across State Biodiversity Boards creates compliance uncertainty . The recognition of forest rights under the 2006 Act remains incomplete, leading to project delays.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
541 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 227 0 R
/T (India's policy architecture is maturing through BRSR Core disclosure requirements and alignment with international frameworks especially TNFD. These regulatory developments are converging with investor action, as demonstrated by Nature Action 100's engagement with companies managing USD 23.6 trillion in assets.)
/E (India's policy architecture is maturing through BRSR Core disclosure requirements and alignment with international frameworks especially TNFD. These regulatory developments are converging with investor action, as demonstrated by Nature Action 100's engagement with companies managing USD 23.6 trillion in assets.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
542 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 227 0 R
/T (The transition toward nature-positive business models requires continued development of measurement systems, financing mechanisms accessible to firms of varying sizes, regulatory harmonization across states, and meaningful engagement with local communities holding forest rights. Early adopters may benefit from regulatory readiness and access to ESG-linked capital as disclosure requirements expand through 2027.)
/E (The transition toward nature-positive business models requires continued development of measurement systems, financing mechanisms accessible to firms of varying sizes, regulatory harmonization across states, and meaningful engagement with local communities holding forest rights. Early adopters may benefit from regulatory readiness and access to ESG-linked capital as disclosure requirements expand through 2027.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [4]
>>
