/Title (The World Economic Forum \(WEF 2023\), report shows climate and environmental risks are now the most significant risks found by global executives for the next decade, but they are also the risks for which we are seen to be the least prepared [7]. Most companies, investors and lenders today do not comprehend their nature-related dependencies, impacts, risks, and opportunities and are inadequately accounting for nature in their strategies and capital allocation decisions. Data released by Carbon Disclosure Project \(CDP\) suggests that 70% of companies showing data through CDP did not assess the impact of their value chain on biodiversity in 2022 [8].)
